GS worker: hand GIF (PATH3) DMA packets to the GIF arbiter instead of copying them again. runGsWorkerJob gathered
each GIF item into item.data (appendGuestBytes) and submitGifPacket(..., false) memcpy'd it once more into the
arbiter's queue. submitGifPacketBuffer / GifArbiter::submitBuffer move the vector in instead. The arbiter gives
those buffers back to the DMA buffer pool through a recycle callback (set by setGifArbiter) after drain() processed
them, so the pool that keeps the EE thread from reallocating and faulting in new pages stays fed; without it the
moved buffers were freed and the pool lost them. The masked PATH3 FIFO still keeps its own copy and the no-arbiter
callback reads in place; in both the item buffer stays with the job and returns to the pool as before. Packet order
and contents are unchanged.
From huanghuangdaquan-beep/gow-native-pc-optimization (its patch 42), rebased on patches 30-45 here; the recycle
callback is this project's addition. Not yet measured on this project's hardware (A/B FPS pairs pending).

